WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
RESPECT.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.960
It's something that I feel...

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.360
...has been lost...lately.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.320
I even feel like the definition of respect
has been muddied a bit.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.900
Because people have
a tendency to apply it

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.680
only to accomplishments
that they feel are worthy

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.420
of praise and admiration.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.580
But, I'm talking about respect
on...

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.360
...a basic level.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.820
Even if you just boil it
down to common human decency;

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.100
It's being lost.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.740
The Golden Rule still applies.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.580
You still need to treat people
the way that you want to be treated.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.140
And you're seeing it
less and less these days.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.040
Because, people
have an automatic tendency

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.400
to assume that if someone
is disagreeing with someone,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.260
they are their enemy,

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.120
and they are inherently bad,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.400
and they should be fought.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.140
But, you can disagree with someone
and still respect them.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.560
You can even hate someone.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.840
You can hate and abhor their actions.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.900
They are doing terrible things
and they need to be hated.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.480
But you still need to
treat them with respect.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.180
And that's hard.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.980
And you may even be thinking like
"How can you do that?"

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.800
"That's not possible."

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.140
"If they are a terrible person
they deserve to be treated unfairly."

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.900
And that's not the way...

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.160
...that I want to live.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.940
We're all humans.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.040
And either we are all
humans that are equal,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.780
and deserve to be treated as equals,

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.220
or we're not.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.340
And I know people are probably going to think
that I am speaking too generally about this,

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.960
so I want to get specific.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.560
I am talking about this because
of the frenzy that is surrounding Felix.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.960
Not "PewDiePie",

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.460
"Felix."

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.500
And I want to be very clear about something,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.400
Felix is not an anti-Semite
and Felix does not advocate hate.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.900
And I am not defending
the jokes that he made,

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.120
because even he has apologized
for some of the "jokes" that he did.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.040
But he, as a person,

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.080
as an inherent human being

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.740
he is not these "labels."

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.220
Because, it's so easy to label someone.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.840
It's so easy to do.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:35.100
It is so easy to boil someone
down to a single word or a phrase;

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.440
and that's all they are.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.040
Even if you are praising them,

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.200
I mean, normally it's when
you're demonizing them,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.620
but even if you are praising them,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.660
even if you are putting someone on a pedestal,

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.220
or if you are calling them "human scum",

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.540
and "trash" and "garbage,"

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.160
you're inherently dehumanizing
them in both aspects.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.140
And that's something that
I will never stand for.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:01.500
Never.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.340
'Cause I have said it a million times.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.420
Over and over, I repeat this all the time;

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.340
We, as YouTubers,
are the exact same as you.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.400
We're humans.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.360
We're...

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.460
...people wandering this world

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.300
trying to figure out who we are,

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.540
just the same as you.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.760
And even though someone like Felix
is being attacked

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.560
and he's a lightning rod for hate,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.320
whether or not that's a fault of his own actions,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.900
or the society that we live in,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:30.580
That

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.300
doesn't

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.440
matter to me.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.100
Because what I'm talking about

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.760
is the most basic human element,

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.320
the one rule I know very deep down,

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.920
is that we are all equal,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.720
and deserve to be treated
with respect.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.520
We are more than our labels.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.760
I don't give a FUCK...

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.280
...what the color of your skin is,

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.440
I don't care what religion
you believe in,

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.640
I don't care where you have come from
or where you are now,

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.520
all I care about,

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.220
is who,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:05.860
you

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.740
are.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.540
And whether or not
you are free to be able to discover that,

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.760
And I am not even just talking
about Felix now,

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.000
I am talking generally.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.060
'Cause if we're ever...

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.700
...going to be more
than we are right now,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.860
as a society, as people, as a species, as Planet Earth,

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.120
if we're ever going to be more than that,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.940
we need to, at the most, BASIC, level...

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.520
respect each other.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.640
And it's hard.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.720
It's hard to take the high road.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.460
It's a lonely road.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.220
No one wants to go that way.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.660
'Cause it is so easy
to seek vengeance,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.300
or apply the "other rule,"

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.660
"an eye for an eye."

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.380
Or label someone,

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.660
as a simple word or phrase,
just to dismiss them.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.480
And, I know,
people are gonna even twist my words.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.520
People are going to say
that I am defending the wrong people,

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.120
or I'm defending "bad" people,

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.900
Or I'm spreading hate indirectly

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.160
because I support other people.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.500
That's not the way I see the world.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.780
I see...

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.140
...each and every one of us.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.480
Not defined by our race, or our creed,

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.540
but each and every one of us
a new opportunity to find ourselves.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.540
And in order to defend that,

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.920
I have to advocate

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.280
the treatment of everyone

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.660
as an equal.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.840
'Cause if you don't have that,

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.700
What's going to become of us?

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.660
What's gonna happen in 50 years,

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.880
when the generations
that follow us look back,

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.820
and see that their forefathers

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.720
were too afraid

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.700
to treat each other with
the most basic level of respect?

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.700
I believe,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.580
I believe very firmly,

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.740
that every single person in the world

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:18.160
has the ability to do something
amazing or terrible,

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.680
to spread love or hate.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.400
And whether or not they do
one or the other depends

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.200
on us.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.680
Depends on us,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.860
being strong enough to take the high road

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.320
in the face of the worst adversity.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.980
I have so much hope

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:38.240
for people.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.400
I have so much hope

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.680
for this world,

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.340
and I have so much hope
for what we can do

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.040
to make it a better place,

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.960
and that's something that
I will defend to the death.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.720
When it comes

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.720
to dehumanizing someone,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:00.860
or anyone...

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.220
I won't stand for that.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.800
Because at the end of the day,

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.080
there's going to be people
that follow us.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.920
And it's up to you and me,

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:20.780
to show them what
respect really means.

